d takes a TextIO file, not a string.","Retrieved v8 migration doc confirms the surrounding v8 API (SerializationOptions, with_meta removal), lending confidence to the family of names but not to 'parses_to_tree' specifically.","The plan feeds captured immutable bytes to the parser (per-call byte cache), so a string/bytes entry point vs a file-object entry point matters for the capture-to-parse seam."],"finding":"The plan pins a load-bearing public API name 'hcl2.parses_to_tree', but the retrieved python-hcl2 source (hcl2/api.py, main) exposes 'parse_to_tree(file: TextIO) -> Tree' (singular 'parse', file-object input). The exact 8.1.3 entry point that returns a Lark Tree from in-memory bytes/string, and the requirement that positions are only populated when the parser is built with propagate_positions=True, are not confirmed against the actual 8.1.3 signature.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f60a059d7ee96cb82","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope > Structural index ('Use public hcl2.parses_to_tree; raw Lark Tree.meta supplies line/end-line/column/end-column')","norm_id":"n693aed03bb4516f4","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer imports hcl2.parses_to_tree in 8.1.3 and hits ImportError/AttributeError because the actual public name is parse_to_tree (or the string variant is named differently, e.g. parses/loads).","Tree.meta comes back empty because the parser was not constructed with propagate_positions=True, silently degrading all line ranges to file-level."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no